          "targetDoi": "10.1080/00140139.2018.1501093",
          "snippet": "The implementation of future automation solutions will reveal the importance of training users in adaptable automation (i.e., selection of the automation level initiated by the operator) and adaptive automation (i.e., selection of the automation level by the machine, for instance based on the operator's attentional state). For instance, Ryffel, Muehlethaler, Huber, and Elfering (2019) recently noted an improvement in the visual scanning of aircraft instruments following a debriefing on performance based on gaze data. However, OpenMATB does not provide any simple way to support studies on self-confrontation.",
          "section": "results",
