          "snippet": "Cegarra et al (  2020  ) then published the independently-developed OpenMATB which was programmed in Python (2.7) and included free software licensing, which allows researchers to run, use, and share modifications to the OpenMATB platform. This allows software extensibility; wherein other researchers can develop extensions and new functionality within the OpenMATB.",
